WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.220
- Back in May, I connected
with Deno Vourderis,

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.440
he and his family own the
Wonder Wheel in Coney Island.

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.500
It's one of the most iconic
landmarks in Brooklyn.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:09.840
I cannot believe I'd never been there.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:10.950
Have y'all ever been to the Wonder Wheel?

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:11.783
Have you ever done?

00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:12.917
- No.

00:00:12.917 --> 00:00:13.750
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh, you have too.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:15.440
I'd never done it either
and I've been here so much.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.300
Like since like, a sophomore
in high school, so fun.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.080
But I'd never been to Coney Island before

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.750
and so, I knew I had to surprise
Deno with a pop-up visit.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.916
So, check this out.

00:00:22.916 --> 00:00:24.026
(swooshing)

00:00:24.026 --> 00:00:27.130
(upbeat music)

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:27.963
Let's do this.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.520
I'm going to go surprise Deno,
he doesn't know I'm coming.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:34.790
- We were lucky enough to be able to open,

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:37.360
thanks to those hardworking,
first responders.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.570
As New York city came back,

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.560
this was one of the
first things to reopen.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.400
- Ready? Okay.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.270
- My favorite part of Coney Island,

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.100
is the Wonder Wheel, right back there.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.466
- Look behind you.

00:00:46.466 --> 00:00:47.886
- What's up, Deno?

00:00:47.886 --> 00:00:50.147
(Deno gasps)
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:50.147 --> 00:00:53.236
I told you, I'd show up.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:53.236 --> 00:00:54.069
How are you?

00:00:54.069 --> 00:00:54.902
- Hold on.

00:00:54.902 --> 00:00:57.370
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.530
I turned around...

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:00.500
And I'm like, I want to say, "Excuse me,

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:01.730
I'm doing something for
the Kelly Clarkson show".

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.177
And it was Kelly Clarkson.

00:01:03.177 --> 00:01:04.010
(Deno laughs)

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:04.843
- How's it been since COVID,

00:01:04.843 --> 00:01:06.770
it's starting to get better, right?

00:01:06.770 --> 00:01:08.950
- Okay, so yes, New York city, thankfully

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:09.890
is starting to get better.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:10.909
- Yeah.

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:11.742
- We're all excited about that.

00:01:11.742 --> 00:01:12.575
You know, they call us, "New York tough"

00:01:12.575 --> 00:01:15.540
and "New York strong" because
we always get back up.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:16.910
- All right, will you take me on a tour?

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.743
- Let's go.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:18.576
- I've heard you have games.

00:01:18.576 --> 00:01:19.926
- We have lots of games,
do you like games?

00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:20.759
- Do you know that I'm competitive.

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:22.310
Did you know this?

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.143
If you didn't know that...

00:01:23.143 --> 00:01:23.976
- Do you cheat?

00:01:23.976 --> 00:01:24.905
- No.
- I cheat.

00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:25.738
(Kelly gasps)

00:01:25.738 --> 00:01:28.020
- Wrong, you are not cheating today.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:28.853
- I'm cheating.

00:01:28.853 --> 00:01:30.410
- I'm going to beat you, fair and square.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:32.367
I was like, so excited to surprise you.

00:01:32.367 --> 00:01:33.794
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:33.794 --> 00:01:35.930
(upbeat music)

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:37.340
Hi.
- Hello.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.906
- Can we play?
- Yeah.

00:01:38.906 --> 00:01:40.785
- Okay, oh, I'm so excited.

00:01:40.785 --> 00:01:43.202
(bell rings)

00:01:45.236 --> 00:01:47.145
(bell rings)
(Kelly screams)

00:01:47.145 --> 00:01:47.978
Yes.

00:01:49.594 --> 00:01:50.700
What?

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.510
- I didn't think she
would be that competitive

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:53.755
with games but...

00:01:53.755 --> 00:01:54.588
(bell rings)

00:01:54.588 --> 00:01:55.610
She's Miss Competition.

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:57.210
- All right, let's go,
let's see something else.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.043
- She really beat you.

00:01:58.043 --> 00:01:58.876
- [Kelly] Good game, guys.

00:01:58.876 --> 00:01:59.709
- Good game, good game.

00:02:00.623 --> 00:02:02.695
(upbeat music)

00:02:02.695 --> 00:02:03.528
- [Deno] Okay.

00:02:03.528 --> 00:02:04.450
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:06.350
My favorite thing I've
learned about this park,

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:07.890
is there was a promise involved, right?

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:08.723
With your grandfather?

00:02:08.723 --> 00:02:11.950
- Yes, my grandfather and
grandmother worked really hard.

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:12.783
They were on a date.

00:02:12.783 --> 00:02:14.490
They used to come to Coney
Island, all the time.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:17.007
And one time he got on his knee, said,

00:02:17.007 --> 00:02:18.960
"I don't have a lot of money,

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:23.530
but one day I will buy you
that Ferris Wheel, over there

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:25.560
and you'll have the
biggest ring in the world".

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.592
- So he got it?

00:02:26.592 --> 00:02:27.710
- And then he bought it and
he had to give it to her.

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:28.900
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:31.070
- It took another 35, 40 years,

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:32.940
but eventually he fulfilled that promise

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:34.680
and got her that engagement ring.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:36.471
- [Kelly] Wow, that's a beautiful story.

00:02:36.471 --> 00:02:37.840
(upbeat music)

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.700
I would really like....

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.800
- Wait, wait, wait, wait,
wait for me, wait for me,

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.233
wait for me, hi.
- What are you doing here?

00:02:44.233 --> 00:02:46.642
(upbeat music)

00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:47.800
- I turn around and see Angie Martinez,

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:48.870
the voice of New York.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.240
- I've never been here,
this is my first time.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.260
- Well, I grew up like
walking distance from here.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:53.550
So, I used to sneak out of my house,

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.970
in the middle of the night and come here,

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:56.920
when my mother was out or sleeping,

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:57.753
I would come here.
(Angie laughs)

00:02:57.753 --> 00:02:59.044
It was the thing, Kelly.

00:02:59.044 --> 00:02:59.991
- That's awesome.

00:02:59.991 --> 00:03:00.957
- [Deno] It's still the thing.

00:03:00.957 --> 00:03:03.200
- It's still the thing?
It's still the thing.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.150
Welcome to New York, Baby.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:06.399
- Welcome to New York.

00:03:06.399 --> 00:03:08.370
(upbeat music)

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.930
Okay, the coolest thing
I love about the city,

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:10.780
you both grew up here.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.840
I feel like there's been like,
so many huge things happen

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.510
in this city, that usually
would break, you know,

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.360
an individual, that usually
would break the spirit,

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.860
but it seems like so resilient.

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:22.050
And that's why I loved
coming here for our premiere.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:24.780
- New Yorkers are the
most resilient people,

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:25.680
in the world, I think.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.320
But even coming here,
to Coney Island today,

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.160
reminding me of when I
came after Hurricane Sandy

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.670
and everybody just wanted to help

00:03:31.670 --> 00:03:33.870
and it's really, a phenomenal thing

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.270
to see people who are going through

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:37.630
the most scariest thing of their life

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:39.400
and saying, "Do you need anything?

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.900
What can I do for you?
How can I help you?"

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.870
- You know, they call us, "New York tough"

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:45.990
and "New York strong" because
we always get back up.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:47.543
- All right, let's go play.

00:03:47.543 --> 00:03:48.690
(upbeat music)

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.060
- [Angie] You go first, Kelly.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.630
- Okay, okay.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.830
- [Angie] Terrible, yes.

00:03:55.222 --> 00:03:56.055
Oh.

00:03:56.055 --> 00:03:58.570
(Kelly and Angie laugh)

00:03:58.570 --> 00:03:59.954
- You got to try to hit the cans.

00:03:59.954 --> 00:04:00.787
(beeping)

00:04:00.787 --> 00:04:01.674
- Get out of here.

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.514
(upbeat music)

00:04:02.514 --> 00:04:04.234
- Oh, that's how.

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.322
- [Angie] I knew it.

00:04:05.322 --> 00:04:07.501
I got to go, I got to go, I got to go.

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:09.092
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:09.092 --> 00:04:09.925
- I love you.

00:04:09.925 --> 00:04:12.023
- I adore you, welcome to New York, Baby.

00:04:12.023 --> 00:04:14.080
- I already knew I loved you,
but I love you more in person.

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:14.913
You're so cool.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:16.950
- Kelly and I were supposed to get

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:18.350
on the Phoenix rollercoaster together,

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:20.180
but then I saw a River come up

00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:21.550
and I said, "This is even better,"

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.300
because that's what Coney Island's about.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:24.790
It's about a mother and her daughter,

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:27.212
sitting on a ride, smiling together.

00:04:27.212 --> 00:04:30.466
(upbeat music)

00:04:30.466 --> 00:04:33.340
(Kelly screams)

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:34.620
- That was awesome.

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:35.453
- Can we go again?

00:04:35.453 --> 00:04:37.260
- That was awesome.
- Can we go again?

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.951
- Can we go, one more time?

00:04:38.951 --> 00:04:40.772
(upbeat music)

00:04:40.772 --> 00:04:42.631
(audience cheers)

00:04:42.631 --> 00:04:45.620
All right, Angie was a
great surprise, right?

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.180
(audience applause)

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.140
She is actually, with
us now from Power 105,

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.271
right here in NYC.

00:04:51.271 --> 00:04:52.572
- Hello, hello, hello, hello.
(audience cheers)

00:04:52.572 --> 00:04:53.692
- [Kelly] It's the voice of New York,

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:55.951
Angie Martinez, everybody.

00:04:55.951 --> 00:04:59.220
So, I warned you that I
could get competitive.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.650
- I'm like halfway happy to see her

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.431
and I'm halfway irritated by her.

00:05:03.431 --> 00:05:04.870
- So, you always have a pulse

00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:05.960
on what's happening in New York

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:07.283
and there's something cool coming, right?

00:05:07.283 --> 00:05:09.190
- There's a lot of cool things going on.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.280
First of all, we just
had a hip-hop history.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:13.170
Well, hip-hop history
month, comes in November,

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:15.010
but around hip-hop, right
now, there's a lot going on.

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:17.150
There's a museum, getting
ready to open in the Bronx.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.350
So, you'll have to come back for that,

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.300
when they launch that and I will take you.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.310
- Momma will show up.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.050
- [Angie] Momma will show up,

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.890
in a hip-hop museum, when it
opens and we'll go do that.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.178
And then we'll play a
game and I'll beat you.

00:05:27.178 --> 00:05:28.011
(audience laughs)
That's what we'll do.

00:05:28.011 --> 00:05:29.427
- You know what? It sounds
like an amazing date.

00:05:29.427 --> 00:05:30.977
(Angie laughs)
I'm in, I'm in.

